  'body-fat-fitness': {"title":"Body Fat % from BMI: Weight, Height & Age","metaDesc":"Free Body Fat % from BMI: enter the Weight and Height and get a body fat percentage of 19.8%. Every step shown, nothing leaves your browser.","canonicalPath":"/fitness/body-fat-fitness","cat":"fitness","catName":"Fitness & Exercise","lsi":["body fat percentage from bmi","body fat estimate without calipers","deurenberg body fat formula","body fat bmi formula","how to calculate body fat","body fat percentage formula"],"aeo":"<h2>What does the Body Fat % from BMI do?</h2>\n<p>Body Fat % from BMI works out the body fat percentage from the Weight, Height, and Age, following standard Fitness & Exercise conventions — the page defaults produce a body fat percentage of 19.8%.</p><ul><li><strong>Inputs:</strong> Weight, Height, and Age.</li><li><strong>Output:</strong> the body fat percentage, plus the intermediate steps behind it.</li><li><strong>Method:</strong> the standard Fitness & Exercise formula, evaluated entirely in your browser.</li></ul><h3>Quick answer</h3>\n<p>With the default inputs (weight of 70, height of 170, age of 30), body fat % from bmi returns a body fat percentage of 19.8%. Assumptions and limits are summarized below.</p><h2>How does the Body Fat % from BMI work?</h2>\n<p>Body Fat % from BMI computes the body fat percentage directly from your inputs — the Weight, Height, and Age feed the formula. Nothing is uploaded: the math runs locally in your browser and the result appears as you type.</p>","desc":"<h2>How it works</h2>\n<p>Body Fat % from BMI is built for body fat bmi questions that need a defensible number: the working is always visible, the inputs accept your own values, and the body fat percentage updates as you type.</p>\n<h2>Using the Body Fat % from BMI</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Weight</strong> — in body fat % from bmi, this value feeds the formula directly, and the steps panel shows exactly where it enters the body fat percentage.</li>\n<li><strong>Height</strong> — in body fat % from bmi, this value feeds the formula directly, and the steps panel shows exactly where it enters the body fat percentage.</li>\n<li><strong>Age</strong> — in body fat % from bmi, this value feeds the formula directly, and the steps panel shows exactly where it enters the body fat percentage.</li>\n<li>Check the result. The body fat percentage is shown as soon as the inputs are valid, and the steps beneath it show exactly how it was derived.</li>\n<li>Iterate. Vary the inputs one at a time; the movement in the figure shows which lever matters most for your body fat % from bmi question.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>The formula behind the result</h2>\n<p>Body Fat % from BMI lists every intermediate step in the result panel, so the derivation of the figure can be checked line by line.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example:</strong> with weight of 70, height of 170, age of 30, this body fat % from bmi calculation returns <strong>19.8%</strong>. The same run reports BMI: 24.2 | Deurenberg formula | Category: Average.</p><p>The steps it follows:</p><ul><li>Formula (Deurenberg et al., 1991):</li><li>BF% = 1.20 × BMI + 0.23 × age − 10.8 × sex − 5.4 (sex: male=1, female=0)</li><li>BMI = weight / height² = 70 / 1.70² = 24.2</li><li>BF% = 1.20×24.2 + 0.23×30 − 10.8 − 5.4 = 19.8%</li></ul><p>Substitute your own values and the same steps produce your answer — that is the point of a calculator that shows its working.</p>\n<h2>Understanding the result</h2>\n<p>The result panel leads with the body fat percentage and follows with intermediate values; if the headline surprises you, the steps usually reveal which input is responsible.</p>\n<h2>Where it helps</h2>\n<p>Common scenarios for Body Fat % from BMI: planning around a target figure, comparing scenarios side by side, and double-checking the body fat percentage. The step list makes it equally useful for learning the method and for double-checking someone else's numbers.</p>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<p>The most common error with Body Fat % from BMI is a unit mismatch — one value entered in different units than its label assumes quietly skews the result. Check each label before typing.</p>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> If the body fat percentage looks wrong, read the steps panel before re-entering anything; it usually shows exactly where the number departed from expectation.</p>\n<h2>Assumptions and limitations</h2>\n<p>Body Fat % from BMI assumes the units shown in each label — entering values in different units will skew the output proportionally.</p>\n<h2>Why use this calculator</h2>\n<p>Because the page doubles as documentation: Body Fat % from BMI puts the formula, a worked example, and the assumptions right beside the calculator.</p>","faqs":[{"q":"What does the Body Fat % from BMI calculate?","a":"This page is a working body fat % from bmi: enter your values, read the body fat percentage, and follow the step list to see exactly how the answer was derived. Because the working is visible: Body Fat % from BMI shows each operation behind the output in the steps panel, so you can verify the result instead of trusting a black box."},{"q":"How is the body fat percentage calculated?","a":"The first steps are formula (deurenberg et al., 1991):, then bf% = 1.20 × bmi + 0.23 × age − 10.8 × sex − 5.4 (sex: male=1, female=0). Rounding follows standard display conventions — the underlying math keeps several decimal places until the body fat percentage is shown."},{"q":"What do I need to use the Body Fat % from BMI?","a":"The Weight, Height, and Age it asks for, or the page defaults if you just want to see the calculation work. Each input maps directly to the formula, and changing any one of them recalculates the body fat percentage instantly."},{"q":"What does the result from the Body Fat % from BMI mean?","a":"The main number the body fat % from bmi returns is the body fat percentage for your exact inputs, and the supporting figures and step list give it context. The model behind Body Fat % from BMI covers the standard case; special cases, edge values, or jurisdiction-specific rules may need manual adjustment."},{"q":"When is the Body Fat % from BMI most useful?","a":"Students, planners, and professionals use it for planning around a target figure, comparing scenarios side by side, and double-checking the body fat percentage, and for sanity-checking numbers that arrived from somewhere else. Bookmark this page — after the first visit it works offline, so the body fat percentage is one tap away even without a connection."}]},
